# head_tail_analyzer

Tube head/tail detection, width, bigger tube, depth X/Y/Z and the trace out of the wrapper.

## Build the wheel
    cd tube_pkg
    pip install build
    Remove-Item -Recurse -Force build, dist, *.egg-info -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
    python -m build --wheel
    python -m zipfile -l dist\head_tail_analyzer-4.0.1-py3-none-any.whl

## Install (GPU machine: CUDA torch first)
    pip install torch torchvision --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121
    pip install dist\head_tail_analyzer-4.0.1-py3-none-any.whl
ffmpeg must be on PATH (reads the 16-bit depth video).

## Run
    python -m head_tail_analyzer config.yaml video.mp4 150 out.mp4
    hta --config config.yaml --video video.mp4 --trace-px 150 --output out.mp4

## Backend
    from head_tail_analyzer import HeadTailAnalyzer, AnalyzerError
    analyzer = HeadTailAnalyzer("config.yaml", preload=True)
    for result in analyzer.process_video(video_path, trace_px=value_from_frontend):
        ...                      # result["traces"][i]["end_xyz_m"]
    analyzer.set_trace_px(new_value)   # user changed it while the video runs
